@tannewt @participant2  I have no familiarity with the CircuitPython codebase - do you have any idea what might be going on here?

@participant3 Your report that it works in a USB3 port but not a USB2 port is quite strange, because Pico doesn't implement the [extra connectors](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/USB_3.0#Connectors) used by USB3, and RP2040 itself only supports USB1.1, so regardless of whether it's plugged into a USB2 port or a USB3 port, Pico should appear identically to your computer :confused: 

As I mentioned above, it's probably better to create a new issue for this, rather than continuing discussion in this now-closed issue.
